From 96fee49dac41ef2ed52b56631dcfe1630cf27447 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 15:16:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 74/75] fix(stuck-agent-dog): live-health re-check before
 mass-death escalation (gfork-nzv)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Graft upstream 329633fc's pre-escalation re-check onto the fork's run.sh. When
the raw crashed+stuck count hits the mass-death threshold, re-probe each
candidate's live health and escalate only on the still-confirmed-down count.
The enumeration scan is not instantaneous across a large town, and an agent the
witness restarts mid-scan must not drag the whole town into a CRITICAL
escalation that SUPPRESSES the very restarts that would recover it. Recovered
agents drop out of CRASHED/STUCK, so they are neither escalated nor needlessly
restarted.

Reconciled onto OUR structure, not a straight cherry-pick: upstream's version
lacks the check-recovery "done != crashed" guard (polecat_completed_not_crashed,
hq-2eqe) and our detailed, fingerprinted escalation body (feryn-l0ga). The
re-check adapts upstream's confirm_polecat_outages to our helpers
(rig_hook_bead/bead_restartable) and reuses the completed-work exemption, so a
done-but-MR-pending polecat is still exempt during the re-check too.

Deliberately NOT pulled: upstream's operational-rig enumeration filter and the
0e3812a6/bd76c2cb doc-contract commits — separate concerns, bigger blast radius,
tracked separately.

Tests: run_test.sh gains a suppression test (agents recover mid-scan -> below
threshold -> no escalation, still-down agent restarts) and a persistent-death
regression test. Red-green verified: the suppression test fails against the
pre-reconcile run.sh for the right reason. 58 assertions pass; shellcheck clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
